{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1791157603035,"sessionID":"ses_ef6b1296effedQPZNncCLx5im2","part":{"id":"prt_109500ad6001kq9NFzkYPbcTc4","messageID":"msg_109500025001m9DvenSfd8MqBT","sessionID":"ses_ef6b1296effedQPZNncCLx5im2","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1791157618802,"sessionID":"ses_ef6b1296effedQPZNncCLx5im2","part":{"id":"prt_1095027b50015hynSRx02Juzol","messageID":"msg_109500025001m9DvenSfd8MqBT","sessionID":"ses_ef6b1296effedQPZNncCLx5im2","type":"text","text":"The reference is consistent. Verification summary:\n\n- `dotenv_values` constructs `DotEnv(..., override=True)`, and `DotEnv.dict()` calls `resolve_variables(raw_values, override=self.override)`. With `override=True`, `resolve_variables` applies `env.update(os.environ)` then `env.update(new_values)`, so earlier file values win over the process environment — exactly what the grader's `values-precedence` case expects (`BASE=file` in stream + `BASE=''` in env → `chosen`; `BASE=` in stream + `BASE=env` → `''`).\n- `load_dotenv` honors its `override` flag: with `override=False`, `os.environ` is applied last so the environment wins; with `override=True`, file values win — matching the grader's `precedence` matrix.\n- The `+` branch of `Variable.resolve` substitutes the word only when `env.get(name)` is truthy (nonempty string), matching the requirement for both env-sourced and file-sourced values.\n- The grader assertions restate upstream python-dotenv precedence and do not contradict the requirement's \"preserving override precedence between earlier file values and the process environment.\"","time":{"start":1791157610421,"end":1791157618801}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791157618809,"sessionID":"ses_ef6b1296effedQPZNncCLx5im2","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"rehearsal_submit_answer","callID":"tool_8oXh8LSiYnVQjkCDZ00kyMtK","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"answer":{"findings":[],"limitations":"Reviewed only override precedence for ${NAME:+word} through dotenv_values and load_dotenv. The proposed reference matches upstream python-dotenv semantics: dotenv_values hardcodes override=True (file values win over os.environ during interpolation), load_dotenv honors its override flag (env wins when False, file wins when True), and the '+' resolve branch substitutes the word only for truthy (nonempty) resolved values. Every grader precedence/values-precedence assertion is consistent with this and with the requirement's 'preserving override precedence' clause; no contradicting assertion or wrong repair found. Parsing/nested-grammar behavior was excluded per instructions and not reviewed."}},"output":"{\"submitted\":true}","metadata":{"truncated":false},"title":"","time":{"start":1791157618800,"end":1791157618803}},"id":"prt_10950459c001COZz35aE6PKoVp","sessionID":"ses_ef6b1296effedQPZNncCLx5im2","messageID":"msg_109500025001m9DvenSfd8MqBT"}}
